# Sprint 6.2 — Session Recovery System

**Status:** ✅ COMPLETE — Build 2026.07.22.003

**Release-blocking priority.** Data loss is unacceptable in an exam simulator.

## Changes

### Level 1 — Transactional Autosave
- Save fires immediately on every meaningful interaction:
  - Answer selection
  - Flag/unflag
  - Guess toggle
  - Confidence rating change
  - Navigation (prev/next)
  - Case navigation
  - Case exam task navigation

### Level 2 & 7 — Checkpoint + Guard Before Transitions
- `checkpointBeforeTransition()` called before MCQ-to-case transition in `render()`
- `guardedTransition()` wraps target with checkpoint + try/catch fallback
- If transition fails, checkpoints are searched newest-first for a valid snapshot

### Level 3 — Crash Recovery (Modal)
- Replaced `confirm()` with a styled modal dialog:
  - Shows elapsed session time
  - **Resume Session** button restores full state
  - **Discard & Start New** clears and starts fresh
  - New CSS: `.recovery-modal` with backdrop and dialog

### Level 4 — Rolling Checkpoints
- Up to 20 checkpoints stored in `cmaP1SessionCheckpoints`
- Newest-first search on corruption (automatic fallback)
- Trimmed oldest-first when exceeding max

### Level 5 — Save Verification
- Every `save()` computes a rolling checksum of session data
- After write, reads back and verifies checksum match
- On verification failure: automatic retry (up to 3 attempts at 1-second intervals)
- Fallback to checkpoint array if primary save is corrupted

### Level 6 — Session Journal
- Append-only action log in `cmaP1SessionJournal` (max 500 entries)
- Each entry: `{ action: 'answer P1-A-001=B', timestamp }`
- Actions logged: answer, flag, guess, confidence, navigation, case transitions

### Level 8 — User Feedback
- 5-state save indicator:
  - 🟢 `All progress saved` (persisted)
  - 🟡 `Saving...` (transient)
  - 🔴 `Save failed — retrying...` (persisted)
  - 🔵 `Recovery used — progress restored` (persisted)
  - 🔵 `Session restored — recovery available` (persisted)
- `persistSaveStatus()` and `clearSaveStatus()` added for persistent states
- CSS for `.save-failed` and `.recovery` status classes added

### Files Modified
- `app.js` — `SessionPersistence` rewrite + save triggers at all interaction points
- `styles.css` — recovery modal + new status classes + `--info` color variable

### Items Changed in Sprint 6.2.1
- Post-recovery user-facing message updated to friendly confirmation: *"Your previous exam session was successfully restored. All progress has been recovered."*
- `save()` now clears checkpoints and journal when the session is marked `completed`, preventing unintended checkpoint fallback after exam finish

### No Changes To
- Scoring, timing, question logic, exam content, analytics calculations
- All validators report identical before/after results

